**What changed**
- **Bigger headers:** hero title jumped to 56px, and every section now has a real 32px heading with a small red kicker above it — much stronger hierarchy than the old tiny uppercase labels.
- **Imagery, all inline SVG (self-contained):**
  - A faint blue/red **node-network graphic** in the hero (fades out on the left so text stays readable; hidden on mobile).
  - A **line icon in a soft blue→red gradient tile** next to each section heading — book/monitor for Overview, target for Goals, calendar for Schedule, document for Assignments, info for Course Info.

Since it's all vector, it stays crisp at any size and adds zero image files to your repo.

Want me to go further — e.g. a full-width hero background pattern, small thematic illustrations inside each schedule row or assignment card, or a photo of you in the Course Info section? And if you give me your exact university blue/red hex values, I'll swap them in.

Locked in: single left spine, date-aware "You are here," short intro → timeline → assignments/info, with five chapter dividers. Here's the full `index.html`.

