<section id="overview">
  <div class="head">
    <span class="ico">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 19 19" fill="#1d4ed8"
           shape-rendering="crispEdges"
           xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <rect x="0" y="0" width="3" height="3"/>
        <rect x="4" y="0" width="3" height="3"/>
        <rect x="12" y="0" width="3" height="3"/>
        <rect x="16" y="0" width="3" height="3"/>
        <rect x="8" y="8" width="3" height="3" fill="#dc2626"/>
        <rect x="0" y="16" width="3" height="3"/>
        <rect x="4" y="16" width="3" height="3"/>
        <rect x="12" y="16" width="3" height="3"/>
        <rect x="16" y="16" width="3" height="3"/>
      </svg>
    </span>
    <div>
      <span class="kicker">About the course</span>
      <h2>Overview</h2>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Computing, technology, and artificial intelligence
      now shape how we learn, work, communicate, and make
      decisions. This course helps you become a thoughtful,
      capable, and ethical participant in a digital and
      AI-saturated world.
    </p>
    <p>
      Over the semester we cover a range of topics: how to
      use computing as a tool to work and create with data;
      how to learn effectively (with and without AI); how to
      find and judge digital information; how to reason about
      the ethics of technology; and how to build a
      professional digital presence for your career.
    </p>
    <p>
      This course is designed for students from a variety of
      backgrounds.
      <strong>No prerequisites are required.</strong>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

