<script>
  // Date-aware "You are here" marker.
  // Runs in the visitor's browser, so it always
  // reflects today's date.
  (function () {
    var today = new Date();
    today.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);
    var stations = document.querySelectorAll('.station');
    var currentSet = false;
    stations.forEach(function (st) {
      var raw = st.getAttribute('data-date');
      var due = new Date(raw + 'T00:00:00');
      if (due < today) {
        st.classList.add('past');
      } else if (!currentSet) {
        st.classList.add('current');
        currentSet = true;
        var badge = document.createElement('span');
        badge.className = 'here-badge';
        badge.textContent = '\u203A you are here';
        var title = st.querySelector('.st-title');
        title.appendChild(badge);
      } else {
        st.classList.add('future');
      }
    });
  })();
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

**What changed, at a glance:**
- **Pixel icons** — every section header now uses a bespoke square-pixel glyph (blue with one red accent pixel): a screen (Overview), bullseye (Goals), ascending path (Journey), checklist (Assignments), bar chart (Grades), an "i" (Info). No more Feather stock.
- **Per-chapter emblems** — each Part I–V has its own 3×3 pixel mark on the rail, a related family with distinct patterns.
- **Timeline** — nodes are now **square modules**, the spine is a **dotted data-rail**, and it's bracketed by a hollow **start cap** and a gradient **finish cap** so it reads as intentional even out of term.
- **Monospace labels** — dates, kickers, the "01–05" numbers, the course code, the "you are here" badge, and info labels now use system mono, giving the whole page a computational voice against the humanist body text.
- **Cards → records** — assignment cards are now links with a mono tag (`A1`, `A2`, `A3 · FINAL`), a gradient top rule, corner registration marks, and a hover lift.
- **Tags** softened from pills to rounded rectangles; **hero nodes** are now squares to match.
- **Hooks added:** empty `st-read` readings slots (auto-hidden until filled), `href="#"` placeholder links on every station title and card, and a new **Grades** section with placeholder weights.

A couple of notes: the pixel icons/emblems are the fiddliest bit to get pixel-perfect without a live render — if any glyph looks off-balance to you, tell me which and I'll nudge cells. And the two cap positions (`.rail-cap.start`/`.end` `top`/`bottom: 6px`) may want a 2–4px tweak once you see it in your browser. Take a look and tell me how it lands.
